From 954c56aaa7e7b06ab883c3f1f0e804b7a9337f4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:11:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] WIP: port blocks, events, loot conditions/modifiers,
 and knife compat items to NeoForge 1.21.1

- Port CantaloupePlantBlock/SalmonberryBushBlock/MiniMelonBlock (ForgeHooks.onCropsGrowPre/Post
  -> CommonHooks.canCropGrow/fireCropGrowPost; the old IPlantable/PlantType cross-mod soil system
  and BlockState#canSustainPlant/canBeHydrated were removed outright in NeoForge 1.21, not
  renamed, so CantaloupePlantBlock#canSurvive now checks sand+adjacent water/frosted-ice directly
  and the getPlantType() overrides were deleted).
- Port SlicedMelonBlock/SlicedMiniMelonBlock: Item#isEdible() is gone (food is a data component
  now), replaced with a null check on getFoodProperties(); FoodData#eat(Item,ItemStack,LivingEntity)
  is gone, replaced with FoodData#eat(FoodProperties) plus the existing manual effect-application
  loop.
- Rewrote EnabledCondition as a NeoForge ICondition+MapCodec (the old Gson IConditionSerializer
  API is gone) and registered it via a new DelightfulConditionCodecs DeferredRegister, wired into
  CommonProxy. Rewrote LootItemEnabledCondition/LootItemBlockIsTagCondition/
  LootItemModLoadedCondition the same way (LootItemConditionType now takes a MapCodec, no more
  net.minecraft...loot.Serializer). Rewrote AddItemLootModifier/ReplaceLootModifier/
  SmeltLootModifier/DelightfulLootModifiers for IGlobalLootModifier#codec() now returning
  MapCodec, RecipeManager#getRecipeFor now needing a RecipeInput (SingleRecipeInput) and
  returning Optional<RecipeHolder<T>>.
- Rewrote ModEvents' addPackFinders to use AddPackFindersEvent's new addPackFinders() helper
  (PathPackResources/IModFile plumbing is gone from that call site); buildContents ported off
  IForgeRegistry/ITagManager to BuiltInRegistries; dropped the Chicken.FOOD_ITEMS/Parrot.TAME_FOOD
  mutation (fields no longer exist, see prior commit).
- Ported ForgeEvents/KnifeEvents/PieEvents: LivingAttackEvent/LivingHurtEvent were removed and
  replaced with LivingIncomingDamageEvent (matching getSource/getAmount/setAmount shape);
  MissingMappingsEvent was removed entirely with no replacement, so the old-item-id remapping
  (aged_fish_roe/aged_prawn_roe -> aged_roe, crystalline_knife, pumpkin_pie(_slice)) is dropped -
  a known, narrow regression only affecting very old saves upgrading through those specific
  renames.
- Ported the knife compat items with Forge event hooks (Knightmetal/Forgotten/Froststeel/Utherium)
  from MinecraftForge.EVENT_BUS/LivingHurtEvent/PlayerEvent to NeoForge.EVENT_BUS/
  LivingIncomingDamageEvent/PlayerEvent (moved package only); ForgeRegistries -> BuiltInRegistries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
